/// known-gap: interp has no decision blocks (decision name ... xx); the interpreter is being retired
/// A decision formula that fails, or gives something other than a number,
/// stops the tick with an error that names the decision. Here a comparison
/// gives a bool, and a bool times a number is a type error.
<>F |
    side: 0
    hp: 10
    decision foe
        targets: F
        score => ((target >> side) != @side) * (target >> hp)
    xx
    judge
        foe and (foe >> score) > 0: hit(self, foe >> target)
    xx
xx
act hit(f, t)
    :say("hit")
xx
a <> F | side: 0
b <> F | side: 1
attempt
    :tick()
rescue e
    :say(:has("{e}", "R1220: decision-formula: decision `foe` of F"))
    :say(:has("{e}", "got bool"))
xx
